.TH READ_COMMENT 3ggl "1 August 1997" "GGL/IGP ETHZ" "GGL Common Lib"
.SH NAME
read_comment \- overread all characters up to a comment specifier
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <common/inout.h>

.RB "int " read_comment
.RI "(FILE *" fpin ", const int " idchar ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function reads bytes from a stream specified by
.I fpin
until it finds a character identical to
.I idchar
or until it reaches end of file.
The filepointer of
.I fpin
will point to the subsequent character of
.I idchar
upon return from the function.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.B read_comment()
returns an error code of zero, when the character was found.
.B EOF
is returned as an error code when
the end of file
is reached or any other file reading error occurred.
.SH ERRORS
The function will call standard library functions
that may set
.IR errno .
If any called function produces an error, or if
the end of file is reached, the return value will be
set to
.BR EOF .
.SH CAVEATS
You have to compile your program using
.I -lcommon
as a compiler flag to properly link
your function to the library.
